1
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,317
Passione is an extensive mafia syndicate.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,797
At the bottom of an intricate totem pole
are groups of six to ten members, like us.

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,317
Above us are the Kapos, like Polpo.

4
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:18,397
Each Cape oversees their
own territory of business,

5
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:22,637
and each team has its focus, be it
assassinations, drugs, or otherwise.

6
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:24,517
While I am part of the Family,

7
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:27,457
I don't involve myself with
other team members and Kapos.

8
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:29,834
At the head of the Family is the Boss.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,257
He has a trusted right-hand man with whom
he maintains exclusive communication,

10
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:37,760
so we have no means of
acquiring info about him.

11
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:43,457
Italian mafiosi hate attracting attention,
as it puts a target on their backs.

12
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:46,517
Even capos will dress themselves
like ordinary citizens,

13
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:49,365
and some even operate
front businesses as well.

14
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:54,500
The boss is the most secretive of
all, and never reveals his identity.

15
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:57,977
Any investigative effort
is immediately uncovered.

16
00:00:58,060 --> 00:01:00,178
I know many who've tried and failed.

17
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:04,100
So, Giorno, if we ever want
to find our man of mystery,

18
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,420
we have to get him to notice us.

19
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:10,377
We have to gain the trust
of someone close to him,

20
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:13,097
or we'll never be able
to overthrow the boss.

21
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:16,437
Our first job is to improve
our standing in the Family.

22
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:18,167
We'll earn the rank of Cape.

23
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:20,462
But you and I can't do it alone.

24
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:22,427
We need a team we can trust.

25
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:25,820
If we want to beat the
boss, this is the only way.

26
00:02:56,880 --> 00:03:01,940
The news of Polpo's demise spread
among Passione's capos like wildfire.

27
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:05,557
The guys in intelligence say
that it might have been suicide.

28
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:07,297
Nah, the big guy would never.

29
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:09,720
Bastard was in a maximum security cell.

30
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,277
No one could get to him.

31
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:13,217
Think maybe he betrayed the boss?

32
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:15,947
You couldn't find a more
loyal Cape than him.

33
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:17,977
There's no freaking way he'd do that.

34
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:22,001
I know, but what I'm most worried
about is who's gonna replace him.

35
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:27,945
I heard through the grapevine
that the capos are Fairy di Dust.

36
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,559
Apparently, Papa committed suicide.

37
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:35,380
Hey, eyes on the road! I got it.

38
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:37,639
Zillard has actually offed himself?

39
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:40,660
I told you to watch the road!

40
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,900
No one knows why he did it.

41
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:47,777
Maybe he was just tired of being a slob,
or maybe life in lockup finally got to him.

42
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:51,331
Whatever the reason, now we
know he was a waste of hot gas.

43
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:55,597
Damn coward bit down on a pea shooter
and painted the walls with his brains.

44
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:56,977
You sure he killed himself?

45
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:59,077
Someone else could have did it, man.

46
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:02,020
Well, the autopsy guy
told me it was suicide.

47
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:06,377
Any expert worth a damn can tell the
difference between suicide and murder.

48
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:07,813
There's a light, dunce!

49
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:13,460
Hey, you know the rumors
about Popo's fortune, right?

50
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:14,930
Rumors?

51
00:04:15,013 --> 00:04:18,274
I know more about astrophysics
than I do any damn rumor.

52
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,360
Before Papa got locked up,

53
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:24,257
he converted some of his cash into
a nice stash of rubies and gold.

54
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:27,105
At least that's how I
remember the rumor going.

55
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:28,926
It's a hidden treasure Drive.

56
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:33,957
He had so much to own not even the bank
or the Family could handle it all No

57
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:38,157
one had the balls to look for it while
the inflatable idiot that was still alive

58
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:40,680
But now he's taking his eternal dirt map.

59
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:45,980
So his treasure is up for grabs It's
free money really and the way I heard it.

60
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,492
He hit five billion lira

61
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:49,740
Are you shitting me?

62
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:56,122
If I picked up that kind of moolah, I'd go
abroad with a bitchin' babe on each arm.

63
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,070
Get real.

64
00:04:57,153 --> 00:04:59,117
I'd rather work my way up in the Family.

65
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:03,553
Once I buy my way to Cape, I'll live
a life most people can only dream of.

66
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,740
But where the hell did he hide it?

67
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:07,786
Isn't there anyone who knows?

68
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:11,885
No, although a thought
occurred to me just now.

69
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,477
The guy couldn't crawl out of that
cell without a crew of helpers.

70
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:18,817
You think an oaf like that could hide
five billion and loot all by himself?

71
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,980
He had to have had some help.

72
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:23,240
Some kind of loyal confrant type.

73
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:26,991
And as we all know, true
confrants are few and far between.

74
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:29,520
Polpo liked Bucciarati, didn't he?

75
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:30,990
Bucciarati?

76
00:05:31,073 --> 00:05:32,820
You mean a tapista from Napoli?

77
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:34,000
That's the one.

78
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:36,355
If he had anyone hide it, it'd be him.

79
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:40,624
And now that Polpo's dead, Bucciarati
has probably made his move.

80
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:44,177
Especially with five billion
lira there for the taking.

81
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:47,731
I'm sure even he has a greedy
streak when he's in the mood.

82
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:49,730
Uh-huh.

83
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:51,840
Hey! Sookero!

84
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:57,537
That bastard actually hopped
his happy ass out of the car.

85
00:05:57,620 --> 00:05:59,091
Did he believe that crap?

86
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:03,740
But if you're gonna try and tell
Bucciarati, I'd be real careful.

87
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:07,240
Word is, he and his
cronies are stand-users.

88
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:11,160
Fugo, can we please be done?

89
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:13,277
It's friggin' beautiful out there.

90
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:16,007
One day away from the
books isn't gonna hurt.

91
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:19,161
And besides, I'm just not
into it today, you know?

92
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,351
Don't say that, Narancia.

93
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,812
You should be commended.

94
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,390
Trust me on this.

95
00:06:26,473 --> 00:06:28,597
It's not easy to ask
for academic guidance,

96
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:31,562
especially when you barely
attended grade school.

97
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:34,836
And yet, you still learned
your multiplication tables.

98
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:36,320
You can do it.

99
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,277
Just remember what I taught you.

100
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:39,301
You've got this.

101
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:42,980
Now then, multiply the six by five.

102
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,720
Six times five.

103
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:46,940
Six times five...

104
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:50,180
Is it thirty? It is! Bravo!

105
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:51,753
I knew you could do it!

106
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:54,037
You're practically halfway to solving it!

107
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:54,950
I get it!

108
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:57,040
Six times five is thirty! Nice! Huh?

109
00:06:57,460 --> 00:06:59,797
Hey, what the hell is this supposed to be?

110
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:00,710
What, that?

111
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:01,857
It's a strawberry.

112
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:04,237
I can see what kind of
cake it is, dumbass!

113
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:07,977
It's not like I'd confuse the damn
thing with a chocolate or cheesecake!

114
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,597
That's not the problem here!

115
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:10,856
There's four slices!

116
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:13,734
They might as well have told us to die!

117
00:07:14,980 --> 00:07:17,300
Another freak out, Mista? Shut up!

118
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:21,277
It's bad luck to take one of the
four pieces, everybody knows that!

119
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:23,536
Making a selection from five is okay.

120
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:25,957
Choosing from three is also a safe move.

121
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:30,037
But picking anything from a group of
four practically invites disaster!

122
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:33,197
When I was just a kid, a
neighborhood cat had four kittens,

123
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:35,917
and one of my friends ended
up adopting one of them.

124
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,297
Well, much to his surprise,

125
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:40,117
that fickle beast scratched my
friend's eye clear out of the socket!

126
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:43,577
Of course, he then beat that
kitty until it was dead and gone.

127
00:07:43,660 --> 00:07:45,601
That's some idiotic superstition.

128
00:07:46,140 --> 00:07:47,552
Just think for a moment.

129
00:07:47,740 --> 00:07:49,564
If you eat one slice at a time,

130
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:52,317
eventually someone will have to
choose one piece from the four.

131
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:53,230
Exactly!

132
00:07:53,313 --> 00:07:57,097
This is when the restaurant staff should
take the hint and bring out three slices!

133
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:59,000
Service here sucks hot ass!

134
00:08:00,460 --> 00:08:02,754
You're more than welcome not to eat it.

135
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:04,950
No way!

136
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:06,977
I demand to eat Tortali Froggerie!

137
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:08,200
I figured it out!

138
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:09,497
All done, Fugo, see?

139
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:10,992
You're finished already?

140
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:12,479
Let's have a look.

141
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:15,370
What's this?

142
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,718
Did I get it right?

143
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:24,920
Fancy little punk shit!

144
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:26,697
You think you can mess with me?

145
00:08:26,780 --> 00:08:30,192
How many times do I have to
keep teaching you this lesson?

146
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,200
Uh-huh.

147
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:37,011
Now he's definitely gone off the deep end.

148
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,985
Hey, Abakyo, are you going to eat
the rest of that cake or what?

149
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:43,200
What'd you call me?

150
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:45,680
A dense kagakatsu, was it?

151
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:48,777
You know, talking down to
people isn't very nice.

152
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:49,800
I'll cut you.

153
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,917
I swear I'll slice you to
pieces for the whole...

154
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:52,920
Dodo bastardo!

155
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:54,239
Enough, you fools!

156
00:08:54,380 --> 00:08:55,321
Get it together!

157
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:58,977
I could hear your bickering
from the front of the building.

158
00:08:59,060 --> 00:09:01,236
You're bothering the other customers.

159
00:09:03,740 --> 00:09:06,357
I've brought along the new
associate we talked about.

160
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:07,780
Pay attention.

161
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:09,620
Don't dishonor us.

162
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,580
I'm Giorno Giovanna.

163
00:09:20,940 --> 00:09:22,822
It's a pleasure to meet you all.

164
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,760
Sorry about that, Fugo.

165
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:28,982
I'm sorry, too.

166
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:31,340
Will you forgive me? Of course.

167
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:34,497
And I promise to study harder if
you'll please keep teaching me.

168
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:35,680
Listen, everyone!

169
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:38,117
I went out of my way to bring him here!

170
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:39,277
Show him some respect!

171
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,190
Mr.

172
00:09:40,273 --> 00:09:41,103
Boucherati!

173
00:09:41,186 --> 00:09:42,016
What is it?

174
00:09:42,099 --> 00:09:43,094
You have a phone call.

175
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,020
Right, thank you.

176
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:48,520
Now then, all of you properly
introduce yourselves.

177
00:09:49,220 --> 00:09:50,050
Capt?

178
00:09:50,133 --> 00:09:51,248
I'll be right back, Giorno.

179
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:54,957
You should get to know your fellow
team members while I'm gone.

180
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:55,870
Sure thing.

181
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:01,197
Giorno, am I right?

182
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:03,297
Don't just stand there, take a load off.

183
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:05,080
Let's have a drink and chat.

184
00:10:05,260 --> 00:10:06,157
They're waiting for you.

185
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,070
Crazy.

186
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:09,161
Bucciarati here.

187
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,430
Understood.

188
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:18,980
Is something the matter? No.

189
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:21,210
Bucciarati.

190
00:10:21,293 --> 00:10:22,123
Bucciarati!

191
00:10:22,206 --> 00:10:23,036
Do you have a moment?

192
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:24,710
Oh.

193
00:10:24,793 --> 00:10:25,700
Signora Menini. Hello.

194
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:27,336
What's on your mind?

195
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:29,917
If you have time, could
you lend me an ear?

196
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,059
And speaking outside would be best.

197
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,793
Yes, of course, ma 'am.

198
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,920
I hope you enjoy it.

199
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:44,300
How old are you?

200
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:45,790
Fifteen.

201
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:47,450
What? Really?

202
00:10:47,533 --> 00:10:49,900
I got two whole years on you, buddy boy.

203
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:51,278
Thanks for the tea.

204
00:10:58,020 --> 00:10:59,260
Is something wrong?

205
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:02,657
You've already expressed
your gratitude for the tea.

206
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:04,740
What's with the sudden hesitation?

207
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:06,980
I believe we're past the niceties.

208
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:08,554
It's time to drink up.

209
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:10,600
Is it not warm enough for you?

210
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:14,697
Maybe he's afraid to down it because
he doesn't want to be one of us.

211
00:11:14,780 --> 00:11:15,610
Huh?

212
00:11:15,693 --> 00:11:19,200
Now what's going on here?
Nothing. Everything's fine.

213
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:23,188
He went to the trouble of making
a special cup of tea for me.

214
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,560
That's nasty as hell!
What'd you do? Speak up!

215
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:36,560
Holy shit!

216
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:38,820
He guzzled down every ounce of it!

217
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:40,997
You're gonna be fun to have around!

218
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,100
Major props, bud!

219
00:11:42,220 --> 00:11:44,357
There's no way you
drank that stuff, right?

220
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,877
Go ahead and tell us how you did it.

221
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:48,237
If you tell me, it'll
be our little secret.

222
00:11:48,320 --> 00:11:49,150
Spill!

223
00:11:49,233 --> 00:11:50,063
Can't recall.

224
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:54,282
But you all are keeping abilities
under wraps as well, aren't you?

225
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:57,660
So this stronzo's a stand user.

226
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:02,300
I transformed my left front
tooth into a jellyfish.

227
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:06,812
And since it's 98 % water, it was able
to absorb all the liquid in the cup.

228
00:12:07,340 --> 00:12:08,457
Can you transport matter?

229
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:09,370
Open your mouth!

230
00:12:09,453 --> 00:12:10,997
There has to be a hidden cavity!

231
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,540
I don't know what it is,

232
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:14,717
but there's something
about Jonah that gives

233
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:17,506
him the unique ability
to charm almost anyone.

234
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:20,360
You think before you act.

235
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:21,440
A smart habit.

236
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:23,151
Have you told Bucciarati?

237
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:24,450
Kind of.

238
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:27,700
We're not exactly a cohesive team yet.

239
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,920
But we have no choice.

240
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:31,022
We have to act.

241
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:33,124
There's no time for indecision.

242
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:34,330
Focus up!

243
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:37,460
We're heading out, so
be ready! Huh? Where to?

244
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:39,580
Just follow me. Come on!

245
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:46,960
Hey, Bucciarati! Good morning!

246
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,057
Have a great day, Signore!

247
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:49,300
Hey, Bucciarati!

248
00:12:49,580 --> 00:12:51,404
Drop by my shop again sometime!

249
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:53,417
I'll have to take you up on that.

250
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:54,330
And the car?

251
00:12:54,413 --> 00:12:55,243
It's handled.

252
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:59,220
Just as I suspected,
people really trust him.

253
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:02,127
Hey, you know there was
no way to avoid that!

254
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:08,017
Bucciarati, this is one of my
dearest friends in the world.

255
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:12,397
Her troubled son has recently started
beating her and she's quite distraught.

256
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:13,310
Aren't you?

257
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:14,980
I see.

258
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:16,517
Well, no wonder you're upset.

259
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:19,120
I'll make it clear he crossed the line.

260
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:20,913
What's your son's name?

261
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,780
Thank you so much.

262
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,720
Deep down, he's a good boy.

263
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:28,460
But those damn drugs, they've changed him.

264
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:33,282
Bucciarati, I've lived in this
neighborhood for the past 50 years.

265
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:36,873
In all that time, I've never
been filled with such worry.

266
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:39,198
What would make him do such a thing?

267
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:41,852
I don't think I've ever been this scared.

268
00:13:42,180 --> 00:13:44,757
Please, you'll keep all of us
safe, won't you, Bucciarati?

269
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:47,252
Bucciarati, you're one of us, aren't you?

270
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:49,560
I need to hear you say the words.

271
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:53,020
Yes, you can rest easy.

272
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:55,340
I'm going to fix this.

273
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:03,878
So you meant we were going yachting?

274
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,040
That's awesome!

275
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:07,579
When did you get a hold of a yacht?

276
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:08,920
We're renting one.

277
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:11,040
We don't get to keep it?

278
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,600
Hey, Bucciarati, hmm?

279
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:17,473
Do me a favor and stay away
from yacht number four, okay?

280
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:19,680
We'll sink to our deaths. Relax.

281
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:22,737
The yacht looks like
it's in tip-top shape.

282
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:23,650
Shut up!

283
00:14:23,733 --> 00:14:25,678
If you like it so much, you take it!

284
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:31,488
We'd like to rent a
yacht if you don't mind.

285
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,620
Prego, prego.

286
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:35,717
Choose whichever one
tickles your fancy the most.

287
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:37,880
Just not number four. I know.

288
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:41,506
All right, we'll take
the one on the far left.

289
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:42,657
Certainly, signore.

290
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:43,975
I'll fetch your keys.

291
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:47,737
I'm interested in renting
the crap for three days.

292
00:14:47,820 --> 00:14:48,980
How much? What?

293
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:52,101
Oh, I could never take
money from you, Boucherati.

294
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:53,820
Use it as you see fit.

295
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:55,180
Crazy mille.

296
00:14:55,460 --> 00:14:56,440
Hey, old guy!

297
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:58,446
Get over here and ring me up!

298
00:15:21,820 --> 00:15:23,540
Ah, yeah, this is the life.

299
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:30,040
Yo, Narancia. Hey!

300
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:31,470
Huh?

301
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:32,870
What?

302
00:15:32,953 --> 00:15:39,000
Oh, well, uh, I was gonna say, hey, I seem
to recall you buying a bunch of drinks.

303
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,677
What would you say to selling me one?

304
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:41,590
What?

305
00:15:41,673 --> 00:15:44,433
It sounds great, but I know
you're never going to pay up.

306
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:45,837
What's the difference?

307
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:46,750
Just give me.

308
00:15:46,833 --> 00:15:48,277
Come on, toss me a cold one.

309
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,301
Why do I bother?

310
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:52,280
You want a cola or a fizzy water? Cola.

311
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:53,980
No, a fizzy water.

312
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:56,396
I want to see all the little bubbles.

313
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:59,200
All yours. Thanks, man.

314
00:15:59,820 --> 00:16:01,820
Here, hold this book for a second.

315
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:05,800
You know, you're the best. Crazy.

316
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,580
Huh? What the?

317
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:16,597
Why the hell did it just stop playing?

318
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:17,937
It doesn't make any sense!

319
00:16:18,020 --> 00:16:19,491
I just bought this thing!

320
00:16:19,700 --> 00:16:20,880
Son of a shitter!

321
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:22,708
That bastard sold me a dud!

322
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:25,237
That cheap geezer isn't
going to get away with this!

323
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:26,150
Hey!

324
00:16:26,233 --> 00:16:29,757
I think we've had just about enough
of the surprises, Bucciarati.

325
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,134
Where are you having this boat take us?

326
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:36,682
We're far enough away that
it's safe to tell you.

327
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:42,917
Our destination is Capri.

328
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,297
What's waiting there?

329
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:47,397
I take it we're not going
for the amazing views. No.

330
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:49,297
So then what's the point of all this?

331
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:50,477
Just lay it on us.

332
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:54,457
This morning the Cape
Polpo killed himself.

333
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:56,037
What? No.

334
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:57,157
That's crazy.

335
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:58,070
You're shitting me.

336
00:16:58,153 --> 00:16:58,983
Why would he?

337
00:16:59,066 --> 00:17:00,760
The why is inconsequential.

338
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:04,616
Polpo was an influential
Cape who courted death daily.

339
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:06,250
Hold on.

340
00:17:06,333 --> 00:17:07,757
Let's focus back on Capri.

341
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:09,157
How are the two connected?

342
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:12,064
Polpo was stashing away
a vast personal fortune.

343
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:13,937
A fortune worth...

344
00:17:14,020 --> 00:17:15,260
Ten billion lira!

345
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:17,920
Ten billion?

346
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:21,237
I'm currently the only one
who knows the location,

347
00:17:21,320 --> 00:17:23,555
as he ordered me to hide the treasure.

348
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:25,780
That lira belongs to us now!

349
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:29,218
With capital like that,
we'll claim the rank of Cape!

350
00:17:30,180 --> 00:17:31,120
Hell yeah!

351
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:34,757
There's no question about it.

352
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,546
My prediction will come true.

353
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:38,397
He's destined to become a couple.

354
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:41,892
This is an opportunity born
of perseverance and hard work.

355
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:44,120
I wouldn't expect anything less.

356
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:46,253
Well, what do you know?

357
00:17:46,700 --> 00:17:48,957
Things just got a lot more interesting.

358
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:49,870
Where is it?

359
00:17:49,953 --> 00:17:52,977
Where'd you stash that kind of
treasure on Capri, Bucciarati?

360
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:54,800
I can't say just yet.

361
00:17:55,060 --> 00:17:58,884
The Family has long spread rumors
about the cache's whereabouts.

362
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:02,354
Until we secure the goods,
we must remain on high alert.

363
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:06,430
Bucciarati!

364
00:18:06,513 --> 00:18:08,008
Hey, something's not right.

365
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,612
Say something, Narancia!

366
00:18:12,860 --> 00:18:13,690
Narancia!

367
00:18:13,773 --> 00:18:15,100
Quit messing around!

368
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:19,073
Guys, you're gonna want to look at this.

369
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:23,180
Just one lone shoe. Hand it over!

370
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:26,137
None of this is making a lick of sense.

371
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:27,120
I don't get it.

372
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:28,977
Where the hell could he have gone?

373
00:18:29,060 --> 00:18:32,577
None of you saw anything
it was quick but it

374
00:18:32,660 --> 00:18:35,097
looks like Narancia was
pulled into this box.

375
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:38,857
The question is how he
went where no that's

376
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:41,617
totally impossible i mean
he couldn't have plopped

377
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:44,257
straight into the ocean
could he Naranja where

378
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:47,760
are you hey Naranja this
better not be a joke?

379
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:50,800
Just say something, dammit!

380
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:53,110
Narancia!

381
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:54,140
Answer us!

382
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:56,270
Mista?

383
00:18:57,620 --> 00:18:59,220
What are you doing, Mista?

384
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:01,710
Mista?

385
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:03,230
Mista?

386
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:04,420
Where'd you go?

387
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:05,660
Not again.

388
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:07,702
Come on, Mista.

389
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:10,416
Don't tell me you're in on this, too.

390
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:13,030
Fugo?

391
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:17,640
Hey, Fugo! What?

392
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:19,150
Oh no.

393
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:22,457
Avakio, Giorno, I need the
two of you to stick together.

394
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:23,658
We're under attack!

395
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:25,520
I'm certain of it now.

396
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:27,200
A stowaway snuck aboard.

397
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:28,680
And they have a stand!

398
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:31,800
But why all of a sudden here? The money.

399
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,110
Yes.

400
00:19:34,320 --> 00:19:37,117
Word must have gotten out that
I know where the treasure lies,

401
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:38,837
and now they're after it too.

402
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:40,685
Someone else from the Family.

403
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:44,397
And how long do you think
they've been stalking us?

404
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:46,357
Is it possible that
they were at the docks?

405
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:47,720
Seems likely.

406
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:52,395
They knew I'd never mistakenly reveal
the secret, so they got impatient.

407
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:56,168
Our pursuer will kill you all
and try to force me to confess.

408
00:19:56,700 --> 00:20:00,777
We're sitting sardines waiting out
here, so they're taking their time.

409
00:20:00,860 --> 00:20:02,677
So you think the others are goners?

410
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:05,920
I'm not saying that, but
ten billion's at stake.

411
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:09,557
They won't hesitate for a
second to kill one of their own.

412
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:12,180
Listen, the others are still alive.

413
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:14,936
They're still somewhere on this boat.

414
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:18,197
I'm not at all certain if they're
being held hostage or not,

415
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:19,868
but they're alive at least.

416
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:22,300
What makes you so sure?

417
00:20:22,580 --> 00:20:24,197
You happen to have any proof?

418
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:26,339
I won't just take your word for it.

419
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:31,077
I used my stand to turn
Narancia's shoe into a fly,

420
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:34,540
and now that fly is trying
to return to its owner.

421
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:39,477
If Narancia had been killed, the fly
wouldn't be hovering and searching.

422
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:40,740
Can you locate him?

423
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:43,680
He's still alive, but
something isn't right.

424
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:47,497
It's not descending into
the lower cabin or locker.

425
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:48,740
For some reason,

426
00:20:48,940 --> 00:20:53,234
it seems to be completely fixated with
searching for Narancia over there.

427
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:55,974
Just what the hell is this guy's power?

428
00:20:56,080 --> 00:20:57,520
Stop talking and listen.

429
00:20:58,060 --> 00:21:02,380
Narancia is somewhere over there by
the cabin entrance. I'm positive.

430
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:07,254
But for some reason, it can't pinpoint
his location, so it's disoriented.

431
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:11,737
We should consider Narancia's location
and the enemy's one and the same.

432
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:14,240
In other words, the enemy is hiding, yes.

433
00:21:14,500 --> 00:21:17,441
But they're not simply in
the shadows of the hull.

434
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,110
Va Bone.

435
00:21:19,193 --> 00:21:21,297
Unless we can decipher
the enemy's abilities,

436
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:24,940
a single misstep could
cost us our lives. Yeah.

437
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:29,257
They may be able to attack while in
hiding, but that's also a weakness.

438
00:21:29,340 --> 00:21:32,634
We'll study their stand and
learn how to take them down.

439
00:21:33,580 --> 00:21:35,660
The real battle begins now.

440
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:41,080
Abakio, our secret weapon
might be your stand.

441
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:43,330
Why's that?

442
00:21:43,413 --> 00:21:46,080
Do you have the ability
to solve this mystery?

443
00:21:49,420 --> 00:21:50,250
Maybe.

444
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:52,230
Habakio!

445
00:21:52,313 --> 00:21:56,597
I hope for all our sakes, you're not letting
a hang-up get in the way of survival.

446
00:21:56,680 --> 00:21:58,033
Is that what you think?

447
00:21:58,180 --> 00:21:59,020
I'm not.

448
00:21:59,220 --> 00:22:01,440
I value my safety far too much.

449
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:04,240
I can't reveal my stand to just anyone,

450
00:22:04,520 --> 00:22:07,940
especially a complete stranger
who has zero loyalty to me.

451
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:13,257
Pucerati, I don't know why you're
placing so much trust in this new guy.

452
00:22:13,340 --> 00:22:16,634
But as far as I'm concerned,
he is no associate of mine.

453
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:20,037
If we don't crack this mystery,
the enemy will kill us all!

454
00:22:20,120 --> 00:22:21,257
And how do you know that?

455
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:24,752
All of that crap is just this
outsider kid's random guess.

456
00:22:24,900 --> 00:22:26,488
It's his cowardice talking.

457
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:28,980
He hasn't seen anything. Habakio!

458
00:22:29,220 --> 00:22:32,900
I bet that bastard is just
hiding out somewhere below deck.

459
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:36,517
I'll force them out here and
give him a helping of payback.

460
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:37,940
Unless you die first,

461
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:41,946
which will likely happen if we
rush in without - Cork it, Kill!

462
00:22:42,940 --> 00:22:45,020
You're just a piece of shit.

463
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:50,960
Come what may, I refuse
to give up my dream.

464
00:22:51,440 --> 00:22:53,146
What the hell does that mean?

465
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:57,000
Go on. Solve it, then.

466
00:22:57,760 --> 00:22:59,300
Don't let me down. Jonah!

467
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:01,092
Have you lost your mind?

468
00:23:07,820 --> 00:23:09,480
No! Giorno!

469
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:14,842
That's where the enemy's hiding!

470
00:23:15,300 --> 00:23:16,130
Merda!

471
00:23:16,213 --> 00:23:17,056
Giorno's in trouble!

472
00:23:18,740 --> 00:23:19,570
Apacchio?

473
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:26,180
Giorno Giovanna, you're one foley idiota
to go to these lengths to prove yourself.

474
00:23:30,020 --> 00:23:32,520
This kid's even crazier than I thought!

475
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:38,720
The marines don't do

476
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:15,680
you?
